WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.855
A vessel develops under moving blood, while

00:00:03.855 --> 00:00:07.160
tiny endothelial projections meet the surrounding flow.

00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:15.705
Transparent zebrafish embryos let researchers observe

00:00:15.705 --> 00:00:19.442
cranial vessels developing within a living system.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:29.399
Primary cilia can act as biological structures relevant

00:00:29.399 --> 00:00:34.041
to mechanosensing. Their distribution changes during vascular development.

00:00:40.383 --> 00:00:44.485
The research combined vascular imaging with systematic

00:00:44.485 --> 00:00:48.587
assessment of endothelial cilia and hemodynamic conditions.

00:00:54.258 --> 00:00:58.762
My contribution was part of a wider collaborative research programme.

00:00:58.762 --> 00:01:03.265
No single clip proves every mechanism examined in the paper.

00:01:09.425 --> 00:01:13.923
Developmental biology begins with moving systems. A still image

00:01:13.923 --> 00:01:18.420
captures a moment, while flow changes the question being asked.
